<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="001" project="spaarke-dataset-grid-framework-r2">
  <metadata>
    <title>FR-01: Add `contentSizing` field to SectionMetadata + wire buildDynamicWorkspaceConfig</title>
    <phase>1: Framework Schema + Consumer Unwind</phase>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <estimated-hours>2</estimated-hours>
    <dependencies>none</dependencies>
    <blocks>005,006</blocks>
    <tags>frontend, typescript, fluent-ui, shared-library, datagrid, workspace-shell, framework</tags>
    <rigor-hint>FULL</rigor-hint>
    <rigor-reason>Load-bearing framework code change to `.ts` files; blocks 2+ tasks; 6+ steps</rigor-reason>
    <parallel-group>Wave 1</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Extend `SectionMetadata` with an optional `contentSizing: 'grow' | 'clamped'` field (default `'grow'` for back-compat) and update `buildDynamicWorkspaceConfig.ts` to apply `defaultHeight` as `max-height` + `overflow: hidden` + `display: flex` when `'clamped'`, or as `min-height` when `'grow'`. Ship unit tests covering both branches.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    SPAARKE frontend framework developer. Expert in TypeScript + Fluent UI v9 + React. Follows ADR-012 (shared component library) and ADR-022 (React 16-safe shared lib). Reads `docs/architecture/SPAARKE-DATAGRID-FRAMEWORK-ARCHITECTURE.md` for context and `.claude/patterns/ui/embedded-widget-sizing.md` for the height-chain contract this task fixes.
  </role>

  <goal>
    `SectionMetadata.contentSizing` field exists; `buildDynamicWorkspaceConfig.ts` applies the correct sizing key based on the field's value; unit tests cover both `'grow'` and `'clamped'` branches; existing sections (no `contentSizing` set) render identically to today (back-compat verified).
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Production use of `ai-spaarke-ai-workspace-UI-r2` surfaced a broken height chain: `buildDynamicWorkspaceConfig.ts:167-171` applies `SectionMetadata.defaultHeight` as `min-height` (a floor without ceiling). Sections grow unbounded to fit content instead of scrolling. The tactical fix (added `maxHeight: '480px'` to 6 registration files) forces 480px everywhere and wastes vertical space on full-page layouts. FR-01 is the framework-level fix: sections declare intent (`'grow'` vs `'clamped'`) and framework applies correct sizing key.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/WorkspaceShell/buildDynamicWorkspaceConfig.ts</file>
      <file>src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/WorkspaceShell/sectionMetadataCatalog.ts</file>
      <file>src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/types/</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-012">Framework changes stay in `@spaarke/ui-components`; no PCF-specific dependencies.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-022">Shared-lib code stays React-16-safe (no React 18/19-only hooks or APIs).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Unit tests are MAINTAIN-class framework-contract tests. No `Mock<HttpMessageHandler>`. No DI-registration tests.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Additive schema — `contentSizing` is optional; omitted = `'grow'` behavior (identical to today).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">No `sprk_configjson._version` bump. Change is in shared-lib TypeScript types + wiring; Dataverse JSON not touched.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>projects/spaarke-dataset-grid-framework-r2/CLAUDE.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-dataset-grid-framework-r2/spec.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-012-shared-components.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-022-pcf-platform-libraries.md</file>
      <file>docs/adr/ADR-038-testing-strategy.md</file>
      <file>docs/architecture/SPAARKE-DATAGRID-FRAMEWORK-ARCHITECTURE.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/ui/embedded-widget-sizing.md</file>
      <file>docs/guides/BUILD-A-NEW-WORKSPACE-WIDGET.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Height-chain contract" location=".claude/patterns/ui/embedded-widget-sizing.md">
        Framework decides sizing; sections declare intent via metadata; overflow lives on the DataGrid's inner scroll surface.
      </pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps>
    <step order="1">Read spec.md § FR-01 + the referenced files above (especially `embedded-widget-sizing.md` for the height-chain rationale).</step>
    <step order="2">Locate the `SectionMetadata` type definition (grep for `SectionMetadata` in `src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/types/` or wherever it lives). Add `readonly contentSizing?: 'grow' | 'clamped';` field with JSDoc comment explaining semantics.</step>
    <step order="3">Update `buildDynamicWorkspaceConfig.ts:167-171` — replace the current `minHeight`-only logic with the conditional: when `registration.contentSizing === 'clamped'`, apply `maxHeight` + `overflow: 'hidden'` + `display: 'flex'`; otherwise apply `minHeight` (existing behavior). Guard against overriding operator-set `style.minHeight` OR `style.maxHeight`.</step>
    <step order="4">Add unit tests for `buildDynamicWorkspaceConfig` covering: (a) section with `contentSizing: 'grow'` gets `min-height`, (b) section with `contentSizing: 'clamped'` gets `max-height` + `overflow: hidden` + `display: flex`, (c) section with `contentSizing` omitted gets `min-height` (default), (d) operator-set `style.minHeight` is not overwritten, (e) operator-set `style.maxHeight` is not overwritten. Test file location: adjacent `__tests__/` per Spaarke.UI.Components convention.</step>
    <step order="5">Run `npm test` in `src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/` — all tests pass, including the 5 new tests.</step>
    <step order="6">Run `npm run build` in `src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/` — build succeeds; types emit.</step>
    <step order="7">Update TASK-INDEX.md: change 001 status to ✅ completed.</step>
    <step order="8">If deviations from plan, document in `projects/spaarke-dataset-grid-framework-r2/notes/`.</step>
  </steps>

  <tools>
    <tool name="npm">Build and test TypeScript projects</tool>
    <tool name="terminal">Run shell commands</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/types/{SectionMetadata-location}.ts (modified — new field)</output>
    <output type="code">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/WorkspaceShell/buildDynamicWorkspaceConfig.ts (modified — conditional sizing)</output>
    <output type="test">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/WorkspaceShell/__tests__/buildDynamicWorkspaceConfig.test.ts (new or extended)</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a section registration with `contentSizing: 'clamped'` and `defaultHeight: '480px'`, when `buildDynamicWorkspaceConfig` produces the section config, then the resulting `style` object contains `maxHeight: '480px'`, `overflow: 'hidden'`, `display: 'flex'` and does NOT contain `minHeight`.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a section registration with `contentSizing: 'grow'` (or omitted) and `defaultHeight: '480px'`, when `buildDynamicWorkspaceConfig` produces the section config, then `style.minHeight === '480px'` and no `maxHeight`/`overflow`/`display: flex` are set by the framework.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a section registration where operator has set `style.minHeight` or `style.maxHeight` manually, when `buildDynamicWorkspaceConfig` runs, then framework does NOT overwrite operator's explicit style.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">All unit tests pass. `npm test` clean.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`npm run build` succeeds; TypeScript types emit including new field.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    - This is the load-bearing framework fix. Task 005 depends on this landing to unwind the tactical `maxHeight` hack.
    - The 6 metadata catalog entries (Communications, Documents, Invoices, Matters, Projects, Work Assignments) get `contentSizing: 'clamped'` in task 005, not here.
    - Height-chain contract is documented in `.claude/patterns/ui/embedded-widget-sizing.md` — required reading.
    - No PCF consumer touch — this is Vite/React 18 in code-page consumption context. But shared-lib code must still be React-16-safe per ADR-022 (no React 18-only hooks).
  </notes>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
    <protocol>Before starting, load all files in `<knowledge><files>`. Follow task-execute Step 0.5 rigor gate — FULL applies. Quality gates at Step 9.5: `code-review` + `adr-check`.</protocol>
  </execution>
</task>
